00:37:38.590 --> 00:37:41.218
remembering how fun it is to...


00:37:41.801 --> 00:37:44.520
just... be lost in it.


00:37:55.440 --> 00:37:59.661
Many of us cling to ideas
that we've come up with.


00:38:00.737 --> 00:38:02.114
We love them.


00:38:03.323 --> 00:38:06.538
We think we've arrived at certain truths,


00:38:06.618 --> 00:38:09.997
but there is so much in
our world that is unknown.


00:39:52.599 --> 00:39:55.936
Travis sent me an email
saying, "You're in."


00:39:56.519 --> 00:39:59.567
All I knew was that
we were going to Kamchatka.


00:39:59.647 --> 00:40:01.991
And it was going to be an epic adventure.


00:40:04.319 --> 00:40:08.574
# Ride all day till the light's gone #


00:40:08.656 --> 00:40:12.536
# I'm with all my friends
Friends, friends #


00:40:12.619 --> 00:40:14.872
# Said I'm with all my friends #


00:40:15.705 --> 00:40:18.709
It's so thrilling to go somewhere
that's completely unknown.


00:40:19.250 --> 00:40:23.220
Eric's the kinda guy who gets
excited by the unexpected.


00:40:23.588 --> 00:40:24.885
He's just down.


00:40:55.912 --> 00:40:58.585
You realize pretty quick
that Travis pushes the limits.


00:40:58.665 --> 00:40:59.791
He pushes himself.


00:41:02.627 --> 00:41:07.348
He puts all of his time and energy
into what he's obsessed with.


00:41:27.652 --> 00:41:30.451
Dude, where are we?


00:41:31.739 --> 00:41:33.412
Planet Hoth.


00:41:34.826 --> 00:41:39.297
I can see wind just ripping,
snow being taken off at every peak.


00:41:40.665 --> 00:41:41.962
We got wind!


00:41:43.292 --> 00:41:44.635
Holy shit!


00:41:54.929 --> 00:41:57.432
The wind's blowing the snow somewhere,
we just got to find it.


00:42:06.524 --> 00:42:08.902
Up top, it's weird crust stuff.


00:42:08.985 --> 00:42:11.658
Up above that, it's wind affected.


00:42:11.738 --> 00:42:13.240
Just trying to figure out what to do.


00:42:21.914 --> 00:42:24.963
This volcano, it's sheet ice.


00:42:28.087 --> 00:42:30.551
When I'm just feeling
like something isn't right,


00:42:30.631 --> 00:42:32.929
it's very easy for me to pull the plug.


00:42:33.009 --> 00:42:36.513
Travis doesn't pull back,
he'll just keep punching forward


00:42:36.596 --> 00:42:39.190
until he gets what he wants
and until there's nothing left.


00:42:40.391 --> 00:42:43.235
I wouldn't have set foot on that volcano.


00:42:46.105 --> 00:42:47.357
Woo-hoo-hoo!


00:42:47.440 --> 00:42:49.308
Yeah, man. I'm ready.


00:43:30.441 --> 00:43:31.317
Dude...


00:43:31.400 --> 00:43:33.277
Dude, that was a burner.


00:43:33.361 --> 00:43:34.198
Seriously.


00:43:34.278 --> 00:43:38.161
Not the worse run of my life,
the worse snow I've ever ridden.


00:43:38.241 --> 00:43:40.455
That was the longest run
in my life, hands down.


00:43:40.535 --> 00:43:42.003
Yeah, it's a long one.


00:43:44.580 --> 00:43:48.918
There are going to be two options,
it's either, we go to the interior


00:43:49.001 --> 00:43:51.220
and try and find some more
low elevation stuff


00:43:51.796 --> 00:43:54.549
or go to beach and go surf.


00:43:59.095 --> 00:44:00.517
Fuck me, dude!


00:44:01.514 --> 00:44:03.937
- What?
- I don't surf, bro.


00:44:04.684 --> 00:44:09.192
Negative 40, coldest day of the trip
and we're going to get in the water.


00:44:09.272 --> 00:44:11.144
Hey, Lando!


00:44:39.385 --> 00:44:42.810
Just being in that cold water
my arms started seizing.


00:44:42.972 --> 00:44:44.519
It scared the shit out of me.


00:44:45.057 --> 00:44:48.311
Those guys like that shit,
I guess, I don't though.


00:45:00.865 --> 00:45:01.991
Fuck this!


00:45:20.426 --> 00:45:22.890
The reason that we wanted
to come here was because


00:45:22.970 --> 00:45:26.516
for years we've ridden Japan,
for years we've ridden Alaska.


00:45:26.766 --> 00:45:29.605
They get the best conditions on the planet,
and then you look on a map


00:45:29.685 --> 00:45:32.275
and you see this incredible
Kuril Island chain.


00:45:32.355 --> 00:45:35.609
It's so good here and it's so good here.
What the heck is in the middle?


00:45:35.858 --> 00:45:40.116
Kurils, it's one
of the most difficult place


00:45:40.196 --> 00:45:42.949
on our planet to organize this kind of...


00:45:43.199 --> 00:45:44.416
operation.


00:45:44.909 --> 00:45:47.207
From our lodge straight to the Kurils


00:45:47.411 --> 00:45:50.210
will be, like, 200 kilometers.


00:45:50.957 --> 00:45:53.506
That means about
an hour flying, 50 minutes.


00:45:54.085 --> 00:45:58.180
But then, from here
to this island, one more hour.


00:45:58.589 --> 00:46:02.435
And some part of the flight,
we have open ocean.


00:46:02.885 --> 00:46:05.138
Sounds like a freaking psycho mission.


00:46:05.888 --> 00:46:06.935
"Psycho mission."


00:46:07.515 --> 00:46:09.237
That's the right word.


00:46:09.317 --> 00:46:10.985
That's the right word.


00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:13.983
You know, weather can change really fast,


00:46:14.063 --> 00:46:16.065
we must be really lucky...


00:46:16.899 --> 00:46:18.071
with everything.


00:46:18.317 --> 00:46:20.695
Hopefully we'll get that
perfect weather window.


00:46:24.824 --> 00:46:28.789
The weather has been beautiful
in Kamchatka.


00:46:28.870 --> 00:46:34.466
We've had negative 40 degrees,
plus 40 degrees the next day.


00:46:41.215 --> 00:46:43.263
So this is calling for Wednesday.


00:46:43.384 --> 00:46:45.478
Thursday, Friday, there's a chance.


00:46:46.971 --> 00:46:49.770
Yeah, the weather's been
like a kick in the nuts.


00:46:50.641 --> 00:46:53.394
When you're hanging out
in the lodge waiting for weather,


00:46:53.477 --> 00:46:55.605
your mind can play tricks on you.


00:47:41.442 --> 00:47:43.160
I don't know, we're just, uh...


00:47:43.444 --> 00:47:44.696
We're here.


00:47:44.779 --> 00:47:45.905
We're in it.


00:47:46.322 --> 00:47:48.575
We're just letting blind optimism...


00:47:50.951 --> 00:47:52.498
rule our destiny.


00:47:57.416 --> 00:47:59.544
We have some news for us.


00:47:59.627 --> 00:48:01.090
Forecast shows


00:48:01.170 --> 00:48:03.634
big, high pressure system.


00:48:03.714 --> 00:48:07.763
That's Kurils. Internet shows,
like one week good weather.


00:48:07.843 --> 00:48:10.638
Classic! Classic Kamchatka!


00:48:11.597 --> 00:48:14.350
You know, we see this,
like, really small window,


00:48:14.809 --> 00:48:18.029
and we finally decided to pull
the trigger and head south.


00:48:21.190 --> 00:48:24.194
There was so much build up,
so much emotion and energy.


00:48:28.155 --> 00:48:30.203
We're like, "All right. This is it!"


00:48:40.751 --> 00:48:42.753
We're going to the Kurils!


00:49:10.489 --> 00:49:12.662
Halfway, you see this current line.


00:49:13.868 --> 00:49:16.417
They're like eight foot
breaking waves where the Pacific Ocean


00:49:16.912 --> 00:49:20.211
and the Okhotsk Sea
are just grinding together.


00:49:20.291 --> 00:49:24.045
To watch that energy moving
across the planet, it's powerful.


00:49:44.982 --> 00:49:46.704
No?


00:49:47.026 --> 00:49:48.699
I don't really know what's going on.


00:49:49.278 --> 00:49:51.280
We can't leave the helicopter...


00:49:52.031 --> 00:49:53.658
that's one thing that's going on.


00:49:54.783 --> 00:49:56.456
Bureaucracy is the issue here.


00:49:57.411 --> 00:49:59.375
We have all the proper paperwork.


00:49:59.455 --> 00:50:03.170
We got approved by the military,
but apparently it's a different military,


00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:05.339
so these guys won't let us in.


00:50:05.419 --> 00:50:06.632
They're shutting us down.


00:50:06.712 --> 00:50:08.134
They're shutting us down!


00:50:08.756 --> 00:50:11.726
We've been detained for, like, six hours,


00:50:11.967 --> 00:50:14.765
but we're just trying to get out of here.
It's a two-hour flight home,


00:50:14.845 --> 00:50:17.974
and there's about two and half
hours of daylight left, so...


00:50:18.057 --> 00:50:19.980
Just trying to keep sanity here.


00:50:21.227 --> 00:50:25.653
# So we made it down
To the Kuril Islands #


00:50:28.317 --> 00:50:30.820
# Had high hopes #


00:50:31.487 --> 00:50:34.661
# But they would not let us
Even past the ropes #


00:50:36.158 --> 00:50:38.497
# Are we ever going to
Get to shred? #


00:50:38.577 --> 00:50:39.703
# I don't know #


00:50:41.330 --> 00:50:42.673
Oh, no.


00:50:44.333 --> 00:50:45.459
# This morning #


00:50:47.127 --> 00:50:49.129
# We thought we were going to
Ride powder #


00:50:49.213 --> 00:50:50.465
Powder.


00:50:51.840 --> 00:50:54.514
# Nah, fool, we're just POWs #


00:50:55.427 --> 00:50:56.724
# Locked up #


00:50:59.890 --> 00:51:00.811
Dude.


00:51:00.891 --> 00:51:01.854
What, dude?


00:51:03.519 --> 00:51:05.691
- Let's make a run for it.
- Yeah?


00:51:13.696 --> 00:51:14.788
That's for you.


00:51:15.906 --> 00:51:17.753
All you guys.


00:51:22.913 --> 00:51:28.044
If we can't ride here, at least
these kids can keep riding here.


00:51:28.127 --> 00:51:30.841
This way we leave
a little piece of us with them.


00:51:30.921 --> 00:51:33.010
Oh! I can't believe this.


00:51:33.090 --> 00:51:36.219
That's crazy,
that snowboarding is alive there.


00:51:36.677 --> 00:51:37.849
Goodbye!


00:51:42.182 --> 00:51:43.980
It's so painful.


00:51:45.477 --> 00:51:47.775
I spent, like, two years
planning this trip.


00:51:48.814 --> 00:51:50.486
We got completely shut down.


00:52:15.132 --> 00:52:17.304
When things don't come together,


00:52:17.384 --> 00:52:20.137
I'm so compelled to figure out
how it does work.


00:52:20.220 --> 00:52:22.018
I dig deeper to find the truth.


00:52:54.171 --> 00:52:58.885
Alaska, it's the place
where it might seem like it's...


00:52:59.218 --> 00:53:01.516
you at odds with the physical terrain.


00:53:07.476 --> 00:53:11.777
But Alaska is really just the backdrop
for you against yourself.


00:53:13.482 --> 00:53:15.905
It's as far as you want to take it.


00:53:52.020 --> 00:53:54.773
It's definitely the driest
we've ever seen it out here.


00:53:55.858 --> 00:53:58.405
I don't think I've ever seen
this much rock in Alaska


00:53:58.485 --> 00:54:00.328
in the wintertime before, ever.


00:54:03.824 --> 00:54:06.789
One of the least amounts of
snowfall in 100 years


00:54:06.869 --> 00:54:09.873
in Alaskan history, so that's kind
of what we're looking at.


00:54:11.415 --> 00:54:13.884
- Holy shit.
- Holy shit!


00:54:21.717 --> 00:54:23.594
Some facets on top of that crust.


00:54:24.511 --> 00:54:25.724
On top of this, ring crust.


00:54:25.804 --> 00:54:27.056
It's definitely scary.


00:54:27.139 --> 00:54:29.517
For the next storm to come in,
we want it to come in


00:54:29.600 --> 00:54:33.020
warm and wet,
rip it out and then snow like,


00:54:33.103 --> 00:54:35.606
you know, quite a bit
on top of that. Would be


00:54:35.689 --> 00:54:37.691
best case scenario, in a dream world.


00:54:37.983 --> 00:54:39.075
Yeah.


00:54:40.277 --> 00:54:42.491
I'd like to live in a dream world.


00:54:42.571 --> 00:54:45.494
Got to tiptoe, unfortunately.


00:54:45.574 --> 00:54:49.420
A little more scary when you
got to tiptoe instead of charge.


00:54:54.249 --> 00:54:57.589
On the road from Japan
straight into Russia,


00:54:57.669 --> 00:54:59.967
came straight up here and, you know,


00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:01.723
just kinda...


00:55:02.716 --> 00:55:03.763
We're just...


00:55:03.884 --> 00:55:07.104
Just battling the whole time,
man, and I just...


00:55:07.638 --> 00:55:09.311
I got to get out of this.


00:55:10.516 --> 00:55:12.518
I can't keep battling.


00:55:23.028 --> 00:55:27.625
I don't know. Big mountains have always
scared me and I have always been able to...


00:55:28.033 --> 00:55:29.997
deal with that fear and just...


00:55:30.077 --> 00:55:34.798
I don't know, there's something about
the snow pack, the low tide and...


00:55:35.624 --> 00:55:39.719
Just something doesn't feel right, so,
I got to listen to my gut instinct.


00:55:41.755 --> 00:55:42.972
Amen.


00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:44.967
- What a whirlwind.
- Go get it.


00:55:45.050 --> 00:55:46.893
- Yeah, thanks.
- Buddy.


00:55:47.261 --> 00:55:48.557
Love you, bud.


00:55:48.637 --> 00:55:50.786
Hate to bail, but I got to.


00:55:56.436 --> 00:55:59.189
One half of me is disappointed


00:55:59.273 --> 00:56:03.744
that a partner of mine
can't meet me where I'm at.


00:56:07.614 --> 00:56:10.458
And then the other side of me
is pure compassion,


00:56:11.118 --> 00:56:13.712
'cause I know that it's
what I'm pushing towards.


00:56:21.169 --> 00:56:23.967
Going over some of the details
of So Far Gone right now.


00:56:24.047 --> 00:56:27.930
Now if the conditions were good you can
knock that stuff out pretty quick.


00:56:28.010 --> 00:56:31.230
Just take a look at these photos from
our scout flight a couple of days ago.


00:56:32.097 --> 00:56:34.520
Yeah, see, if you look at
photos from last year.


00:56:34.600 --> 00:56:37.854
You know, all this is, like,
rideable, filled in, like...


00:56:37.978 --> 00:56:41.198
It takes a season's worth of snow for
So Far Gone, I don't think that's happening.


00:56:41.857 --> 00:56:46.779
You know, we kinda got a long game
with the plan and this area


00:56:46.862 --> 00:56:49.536
and seeing as how this year is already
really challenging out there,


00:56:50.073 --> 00:56:53.998
and not looking all that safe from what
we've been able to collect so far.


00:56:54.244 --> 00:56:56.061
Maybe we go out next year


00:56:56.142 --> 00:56:59.375
when we hope conditions
are better than they are this year.


00:57:00.125 --> 00:57:01.968
We grow into that.


00:57:02.794 --> 00:57:04.296
It was looking really bleak.


00:57:04.379 --> 00:57:06.302
We were talking about
pulling out of the field.


00:57:06.423 --> 00:57:10.389
We did two weeks waiting
for a good snow and then we saw


00:57:10.469 --> 00:57:13.809
a mass of low pressure,
way off the Aleutians,


00:57:13.889 --> 00:57:16.483
coming from Russia
and watched it for days,


00:57:17.768 --> 00:57:21.693
and it just turned into this incredible,
stable snowpack.


00:57:22.731 --> 00:57:24.653
So Far Gone is not happening,


00:57:24.733 --> 00:57:28.533
but there are places that
you can go and still find...


00:57:28.904 --> 00:57:30.372
somewhat normal conditions.


00:57:32.741 --> 00:57:35.414
So it's just the two of us, so we're gonna


00:57:35.494 --> 00:57:37.708
definitely be shredding
with the third in spirit.


00:57:37.788 --> 00:57:38.630
Yeah.


00:57:38.747 --> 00:57:39.835
Um...


00:57:39.915 --> 00:57:46.133
But, you know, a little bummed
that he had to, he had to bounce.


00:58:44.187 --> 00:58:45.150
Looks like AK.


00:58:45.230 --> 00:58:47.069
I'm scared, finally.


01:00:06.937 --> 01:00:08.400
You've got to cross the slough.


01:00:08.480 --> 01:00:10.574
I was thinking about coming
in the middle here.


01:01:44.910 --> 01:01:49.831
Travis pushes the limit so hard,
but when we look at decisions that he makes,


01:01:50.373 --> 01:01:51.625
they're very calculated.


01:01:52.042 --> 01:01:54.965
That's probably what
I respect the most about him.


01:01:55.045 --> 01:01:57.423
He sees that he could ride it and he will.


01:02:04.304 --> 01:02:06.577
Trav, you got this, buddy!


01:04:03.673 --> 01:04:05.016
- Dropping.
- Go on, man.


01:04:50.428 --> 01:04:52.146
Look at that, buddy. Get this. Get this!


01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:54.732
Oh!


01:04:55.350 --> 01:04:57.419
Yeah!


01:04:57.936 --> 01:04:59.849
Good job, boys.


01:05:00.897 --> 01:05:02.524
That makes it all worth it, right there.


01:05:03.274 --> 01:05:05.026
- Amen.
- That's what we live for.


01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:07.487
A beautiful day.


01:05:07.570 --> 01:05:09.789
Seriously. Yeah, buddy.


01:05:12.367 --> 01:05:14.040
You land things and you don't land things.


01:05:14.828 --> 01:05:17.239
I guess if you're Travis,
you usually land things


01:05:17.320 --> 01:05:19.625
that you probably shouldn't have landed.


01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:42.105
The fragment's the size of my finger.


01:05:42.188 --> 01:05:44.861
The CAT scan on top of the MRI
shows a little old injury


01:05:44.941 --> 01:05:46.864
and then the new injury
on top of the old injury.


01:05:47.277 --> 01:05:48.278
No question.


01:05:50.113 --> 01:05:53.242
On the right side that's normal
volume to the nerve holes,


01:05:54.033 --> 01:05:56.661
but if you look at the left side
almost all of its disc.


01:05:57.412 --> 01:06:00.291
Most people would be laying on the floor,
carrying him on an ironing board.


01:06:00.373 --> 01:06:03.126
They wouldn't be up walking around
smiling with that kind of rupture.


01:06:03.209 --> 01:06:08.047
If you look at this, which is the paraspinous
muscle and the belly muscle, the soleus.


01:06:08.131 --> 01:06:09.849
His muscles around his spine


01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:12.184
are the single biggest ones
I've ever seen.


01:06:12.343 --> 01:06:14.971
His core muscles
are literally like this...


01:06:15.054 --> 01:06:17.852
- I mean, I've never see this. It's insane.
- It's huge.


01:06:17.932 --> 01:06:22.607
Travis Rice, a left L 4-5
posterior lumbar microdiscectomy.


01:06:22.687 --> 01:06:26.442
No known drug allergies,
two grams of Ancef is in.


01:06:40.246 --> 01:06:41.589
What's the fourth phase?


01:06:42.624 --> 01:06:45.468
When water meets a surface,


01:06:45.710 --> 01:06:48.463
the molecules undergo massive change.


01:06:50.381 --> 01:06:52.850
They become structured,


01:06:53.927 --> 01:06:56.021
they acquire charge...


01:06:57.263 --> 01:06:59.357
All you need is light.


01:07:00.308 --> 01:07:02.777
Waking up. The surgery is done.
Went perfect.


01:07:03.311 --> 01:07:04.649
You in there?


01:07:04.729 --> 01:07:05.855
Open your eyes up.


01:07:05.939 --> 01:07:07.156
You're going to be back.


01:07:18.368 --> 01:07:23.248
When we set out on a goal,
follow through means a lot,


01:07:24.123 --> 01:07:25.921
and you push it a lot,


01:07:27.043 --> 01:07:30.263
regardless of how
the outcome might end up.


01:08:28.563 --> 01:08:29.530
Yep.


01:08:48.124 --> 01:08:51.594
My phone rings and I was like,
"Why is Travis Rice calling me,


01:08:51.711 --> 01:08:54.926
telling me all about his trip,"
and he wants to go to the sickest place


01:08:55.006 --> 01:08:56.349
he's ever seen in Alaska.


01:08:56.758 --> 01:08:58.010
Then at some point he tells me,


01:08:58.176 --> 01:09:00.395
"Yeah, I would be stoked
if you could join in."


01:09:00.511 --> 01:09:02.184
I could not truly believe it.


01:09:02.722 --> 01:09:05.726
So Far Gone finally feels
like it's coming into alignment,


01:09:05.808 --> 01:09:11.189
but living and snowboarding in an area like
this comes with a lot of heavy exposure.


01:09:11.522 --> 01:09:15.993
I'm just gonna get my legs and mind
warmed up to this style of riding again,


01:09:16.277 --> 01:09:18.779
reconnect with
the mountains here in Alaska.


01:09:25.536 --> 01:09:27.504
In Valdez, perfect warm up


01:09:27.622 --> 01:09:30.922
before a big mission in the glaciers.


01:09:43.554 --> 01:09:46.057
I don't feel like I chose Victor,


01:09:46.933 --> 01:09:49.480
it's what he's done in snowboarding,


01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:52.484
the ways he's tried
to express his own riding.


01:09:53.189 --> 01:09:55.442
He wrote his own destiny.


01:10:00.738 --> 01:10:04.912
Victor in three... two... one... dropping!


01:10:22.677 --> 01:10:23.803
Travis, dropping.


01:10:39.402 --> 01:10:41.090
That's it.


01:10:58.838 --> 01:11:00.181
Victor and his French rules.


01:12:02.318 --> 01:12:04.491
It's been about ten years
since I went out with Jones


01:12:04.612 --> 01:12:06.159
and camped on a glacier for a month


01:12:06.239 --> 01:12:09.994
and totally changed my perspective
on ways to operate up here in Alaska.


01:12:11.077 --> 01:12:13.671
It's great to have him up here
so we can kinda get aligned for


01:12:14.080 --> 01:12:15.457
our approach into So Far Gone.


01:12:15.748 --> 01:12:18.172
Jeremy Jones, and he's right there.


01:12:18.751 --> 01:12:20.594
Rice, I'm 100 percent.


01:12:20.753 --> 01:12:21.674
Copy that.


01:12:21.754 --> 01:12:22.630
Give her heaven, buddy.


01:13:38.497 --> 01:13:39.965
Fuck, yeah. Dude, get this.


01:14:03.773 --> 01:14:05.116
Good job, Victor.


01:14:06.150 --> 01:14:08.903
Travis, just give me a circle
when you're ready.


01:14:09.028 --> 01:14:11.747
Three... two... one...


01:14:12.323 --> 01:14:13.825
Travis, dropping.


01:15:58.304 --> 01:16:01.683
I find myself infatuated...


01:16:02.725 --> 01:16:07.276
with a vision of doing something
in such a specific way.


01:16:22.036 --> 01:16:24.960
I have not figured out how to separate...


01:16:27.875 --> 01:16:29.718
reckless optimism...


01:16:34.423 --> 01:16:37.427
from a healthy appetite to pursue things,


01:16:37.927 --> 01:16:40.225
until it becomes impossible.


01:16:43.307 --> 01:16:46.231
To be able to know the difference...


01:16:50.064 --> 01:16:52.066
Yeah, it'd be amazing.


01:16:58.072 --> 01:17:01.830
I've been lucky to have
a few glimpses into...


01:17:02.493 --> 01:17:05.212
what this idea of letting go really is.


01:17:10.167 --> 01:17:12.010
I know it's possible.


01:19:26.553 --> 01:19:30.600
I was laying there, very upset
with the decisions I made.


01:19:30.683 --> 01:19:34.062
Angry that I'd just injured myself,


01:19:35.312 --> 01:19:41.493
knowing that So Far Gone wasn't
going to happen, and I had a shift.


01:19:41.735 --> 01:19:46.115
I was given this gift of humility
and appreciation for life.


01:19:47.950 --> 01:19:52.872
And everything that happens to me
is this opportunity for learning.


01:19:52.955 --> 01:19:55.083
Really, the greatest journey


01:19:55.165 --> 01:19:58.836
is the one that you take towards
a better understanding of yourself


01:19:58.919 --> 01:20:01.342
and this incredible life


01:20:01.588 --> 01:20:02.885
that we get to live.


01:20:06.802 --> 01:20:08.520
Now we get the wind back.


01:20:11.890 --> 01:20:12.766
Okay.


01:20:13.600 --> 01:20:15.102
There she is.


01:21:31.178 --> 01:21:32.179
Yay, Lando!


01:22:31.071 --> 01:22:32.243
Fuck, yeah, Rice.


01:22:32.364 --> 01:22:34.386
You're gonna be bouncing right over.


01:22:40.247 --> 01:22:44.127
We feel free when a new
understanding appears.


01:22:47.087 --> 01:22:49.385
So, that's where we get great pleasure.


01:22:51.884 --> 01:22:55.229
We stumble and we try and finally
something comes together.


01:22:56.763 --> 01:22:58.765
It's beautiful.


01:23:24.166 --> 01:23:26.339
This process we follow...


01:23:38.013 --> 01:23:40.141
This cycle we ride.


01:25:20.532 --> 01:25:24.081
There was a series of letters
from Einstein to his daughter,


01:25:24.161 --> 01:25:28.257
and they weren't to be released
until many years after her death.


01:25:28.540 --> 01:25:30.587
And one of them was a charming story,


01:25:30.667 --> 01:25:33.671
he said, "Take my equation, E = mc2


01:25:34.171 --> 01:25:37.471
and replace the 'm,'
replace the mass with love."


01:25:38.050 --> 01:25:40.428
He said, "You put love into the equation,


01:25:40.510 --> 01:25:44.184
and love times the speed of
light square gives you energy."


01:25:44.264 --> 01:25:47.108
He says, "The real energy
comes from love."


01:25:55.692 --> 01:25:58.156
Who's got a phone? I have to call my mom.


01:25:58.236 --> 01:26:01.410
Mom. Hey, Mom. Yeah, can you hear me?


01:26:01.490 --> 01:26:03.704
Hey, I did it.


01:26:03.784 --> 01:26:06.128
Huh? No, no, no, she's not pregnant.


01:26:06.286 --> 01:26:09.084
I mean snowboarding.
I couldn't have done it without you.


01:26:09.164 --> 01:26:10.752
All right, ma. I got to go.


01:26:10.832 --> 01:26:12.926
All right. Love you. No, you hang up.


01:26:19.925 --> 01:26:22.514
Two ducks in a pond and a burned out belt.


01:26:22.594 --> 01:26:23.891
It's the way to start the morning.


01:26:24.012 --> 01:26:25.309
We need to reinvent ourselves.


01:26:25.389 --> 01:26:27.227
I'm gonna dye my hair
and start doing one foot tricks.


01:26:27.307 --> 01:26:30.355
I'm going to grow a beard
and just be a sarcastic asshole.


01:26:30.936 --> 01:26:32.758
Has anyone seen Wheeler?


01:26:35.941 --> 01:26:38.285
Just got back from battle, dude.


01:26:38.402 --> 01:26:40.029
That's what it's all about, boys.


01:26:40.445 --> 01:26:43.164
Watch out for this guy, he's straight up.


01:26:43.907 --> 01:26:45.454
Flippin' that, flippin' this.


01:26:45.575 --> 01:26:48.545
These fans are going to get goin'.
All this stuff's gonna light up,


01:26:48.662 --> 01:26:50.756
so I don't want you
to be freaked out by that.


01:26:50.872 --> 01:26:53.211
We're gonna serve lunch
right on the tip top


01:26:53.291 --> 01:26:55.134
of that volcano up there.


01:26:55.252 --> 01:26:58.552
Spewing hot lava,
we're gonna have hot soup,


01:26:58.880 --> 01:27:02.054
hot coffee, that's gonna be
hot shit right now.


01:27:02.134 --> 01:27:04.056
Captain, I think
we're about ready to take off.


01:27:04.136 --> 01:27:06.138
We gotta go now!


01:27:16.273 --> 01:27:17.775
The course is ready.


01:27:20.861 --> 01:27:21.987
There comes the vibe.


01:27:22.070 --> 01:27:23.116
Thanks, guys.


01:27:23.196 --> 01:27:26.245
We are deep in the mountains
that we've hiked for two days.


01:27:26.366 --> 01:27:29.711
It's rugged conditions out there,
way worse than when Jeremy Jones was here.


01:27:29.828 --> 01:27:32.001
It's burlap sack out there, bro.


01:27:39.337 --> 01:27:41.510
- Tell me when it's in the right spot.
- All right.


01:27:44.551 --> 01:27:46.804
Yeah, that's how you block.


01:27:47.137 --> 01:27:51.062
I gotta let the big dogs eat, then
the little, small dog can eat after that.


01:27:51.183 --> 01:27:52.730
Just like the X Games right, bud?


01:27:52.851 --> 01:27:54.979
Just have someone else build you a park.


01:27:58.440 --> 01:28:02.294
The jump would be finished if you
were shoveling, not filming nothing.


01:28:02.819 --> 01:28:04.866
The crew is really fired up
for this mission.


01:28:04.946 --> 01:28:06.744
Everything's really starting
to make sense.


01:28:06.990 --> 01:28:09.955
And I think, even back at home
people are gonna be really impressed


01:28:10.035 --> 01:28:12.037
by what we're gonna bring home.


01:28:14.623 --> 01:28:17.295
Yeah, I'm in the field.
Listen, we got an emergency.


01:28:17.375 --> 01:28:19.002
Listen, I know you're just sitting there.


01:28:19.085 --> 01:28:22.089
No, we're just looking for gnarly
conditions, one way or the other.


01:28:22.464 --> 01:28:23.716
Earn your keep.


01:28:26.343 --> 01:28:29.222
I was bored a couple of years back,
decided to go to flight school.


01:28:29.471 --> 01:28:32.761
Fly around them long enough,
you want to be able to fly one.


01:28:48.490 --> 01:28:50.788
Yeah, you know,
things are different these days.


01:28:50.909 --> 01:28:53.662
You can't just roam around
the streets of Tokyo,


01:28:53.745 --> 01:28:57.045
with your GoPro 3, ah, 3.5,


01:28:57.499 --> 01:29:01.923
thinking you're going to get a freaking
viral video to go past 0.5 million.


01:29:04.548 --> 01:29:05.970
Welcome to Alaska.


01:29:06.216 --> 01:29:08.310
Let the games begin!


01:29:26.361 --> 01:29:28.238
Hell, yeah, slapstick.


01:29:29.447 --> 01:29:33.327
We got Scott Serfas and Mark Landvik
versus Travis Rice and Eric Jackson.


01:29:33.618 --> 01:29:36.087
Little two-on-two, half court press.


01:29:36.413 --> 01:29:37.710
What you gonna do, bitch?


01:29:39.833 --> 01:29:41.885
All right, Trav. Let's do this.


01:30:01.771 --> 01:30:03.819
Marquesas Dead ahead!


01:30:06.607 --> 01:30:11.078
We want to find snow!
We gotta go that way!


01:30:11.821 --> 01:30:13.038
West!


01:30:13.948 --> 01:30:16.417
No, left, you idiot!


01:30:16.951 --> 01:30:18.544
That way.


01:30:18.744 --> 01:30:20.997
Is that all you've got?


01:30:21.706 --> 01:30:23.458
Bring it on!

